diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b5fe1b2a4feac926b16f4b55fd72f2bb6eb7b711..ca001d7c4d7b58bd7d3f247c062177d581b97a8b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,23 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental module
+
+`src/index.ts` exports `createRentalService()`, an in-memory service that rents boards and sails.
+Its state is lost when the process stops; persistence comes later.
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` adds an item. `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }` without reserving anything.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` reserves the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+The school's rules, which apply to every operation:
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are UTC ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A period covers whole days: it starts and ends at midnight UTC, and `end` is the start of the day
+   after the last rented day. Periods are half-open, so one booking may start on the day another ends.
+4. An item cannot be booked for overlapping periods. `quote` does not check availability; `book` does.
+5. Cancellation policy: not implemented yet.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` and the type-check with `npm run typecheck`.
